      "id": 1,
      "text": "Knotts Island began as Maun's Island in 1820 before relocating to its current spot in 1855 by Jackson Spratt.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://northcarolinatraveler.com/knotts-island-nc/",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The island sits within Currituck Sound, bordered by North Landing River, Back Bay, and Knotts Island Bay.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        14
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Knotts_Island%2C_North_Carolina",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Mackay Island National Wildlife Refuge borders the island, offering rich marsh habitats for birds and wildlife.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        15
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Knotts_Island%2C_North_Carolina",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "A free ferry operated by the North Carolina Department of Transportation links Knotts Island to Currituck mainland every day.",
